% layout 'outsider';
% title "Explain the service login button";

<h1>Login via Open Console</h1>

<div class="container">
  <div class="card" id="login-card">
    <h5 class="card-header">Context</h5>
    <div class="card-body">

<p>When you are the owner of a service, offered via the public web,
and you wish to implement a "Login via Open Console" button, then this
page will show you how.</p>

<p>First some context:</p>
<ul>
<li>This page explains the "Open Console Client" which needs to become part of your application.  It is
    all JSON communication, so very simple to process.</li>
<li>The technical specification can be found at the
    <a href="https://github.com/Skrodon/open-console-connect/wiki/">Open Console Connect wiki</a>.
    Below, you only find an example of the global flow.</li>
</ul>

    </div>
  </div>
</div>

&nbsp;

<div class="container">
  <div class="card" id="login-card">
    <h5 class="card-header">Preparation</h5>
    <div class="card-body">

<p>You will need to take the following stepts to define your service inside Open Console:</p>
<ol>
<li>Create a personal account in Open Console;</li>
<li>Create an identity in that account, which relates to your service;</li>
<li>Create or join a group with that identity;</li>
<li>Proof ownership to the website which runs your service;</li>
<li>Create a service description in that group.</li>
</ol>

<p>This results in a service identifier (a token "*:S:*"), and a secret you have chosen
(more like a password).</p>

    </div>
  </div>
</div>

&nbsp;

<div class="container">
  <div class="card" id="login-card">
    <h5 class="card-header">Connect your instance</h5>
    <div class="card-body">

<p>When your application starts, it needs to register itself at
Open Console.  Every instance (every host) should login separately.
Returned is
<a href="https://github.com/Skrodon/open-console-connect/wiki/Application-Session#logging-in-for-the-application">a
complex session structure</a>, which you need to save in your database.

<p>At the moment, there is only one reference implementation: for the
Mojolicious framework for Perl.  You will probably understand it, even
when you do not know any Perl.  Please, consider to release code which
does the same for your framework on your programming language.
<a href="https://metacpan.org/release/Mojolicious-Plugin-OpenConsole" target="blank">Mojolicious::Plugin::OpenConsole</a>.
Please consider to publish your implementation, in the language of your choice.</p>

% my $s = $c->OpenConsole->buttonSetup;
<style>.oc-logo { height: 30px; width: 30px; background: white; padding: 3px; margin: 5px }</style>
<button class="btn btn-primary oc_login_button"
  onClick="window.location='/client/login?app=<%= $s->{client_id} %>'">
   <span><%== $s->{logo_svg} %></span>
   Login via OpenConsole
</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
